    "notes": "A long, gentle, deliberately cool drink — about 90 g out, served warm rather than hot.\n\nTwo minutes of contact at low flow: a two-second temperature-compensation fill and then a full 60 seconds of puck wetting at 2 ml/s, both at 86.5 → 81.5 °C and both exiting early if pressure passes 5 bar. The final frame runs 60 seconds at 3 ml/s under a 2 bar ceiling.\n\nThat last frame is set to 10 °C, which looks like an error and is not. The DE1 cannot chill water, so a target below tank temperature simply means *no heating* — the machine delivers water as cool as it can. Applied across most of a 90 g yield it pulls the cup temperature well down, which is what the 58 in the name refers to. Leave it alone unless you want a hotter drink; raising it is the knob for that.\n\n(Bundled from the Decaid default set, author Rohan. It shipped without notes; the description above is read from the profile's own frames.)",
